descriptionByLocale.en:
PUBLIC CONCOURSE FOR PERSONAL ASSESSMENT The Ente Case Anziani Mendrisiotto ECAM, communicates the reopening of the terms of submission of applications for the public contest, FU of 22.06.2026, for the recruitment of: a/a Capostructure at the Casa Anziani Santa Lucia (Arzo) 100% Tasks

• conduct a House for the elderly, with specific tasks in the management of/workers and

collaborators in a public context and orienting their action to organizational well-being;

• promote the well-being of residents in compliance with the mission of network institutions

ECAM, current regulations and ethical values that distinguish the offer of services in the Houses;

• enhance available resources and optimize collaborations with other Network Houses in order

to promote the improvement of the structure in an economic perspective of scale;

• promote synergies between the Network Houses and promote network development;

• activate the network of external territorial services, families and people close to/from residents

to ensure the best quality of life possible;

• manage the activities of the care sector and all the services of the structure according to work plans,

internal organisational arrangements, indications of the administrative and health management and quota requirements. Formal requirements

• CRS training 3/4 years (or equivalent/superior qualifications);

• SUP diploma (Master of Advances Studies, MAS in Health Management) or availability at

achievement within 3 years;

• experience of responsibility in managing aspects related to department management or

care of a health or social structure of the Canton Ticino, preferably in a CPA of the ECAM network (constitutes preferential element);

• knowledge of the RAI system (Q-Sys) and the resource calculation system;

• residence in the Canton of Ticino (constitutes preferential element);

• Italian mother tongue and knowledge of a second national language (constitutes element

preferential);

• knowledge of the cantonal and federal health and sociosanitary system.

Aptitude requirements

• listening and relationship skills;

• management, coordination and motivation of employees and collaborators;

• good communication skills, sensitivity, availability, spirit of initiative, attitude to work

individual and group and openness to comparison;

• guidance on objectives and results;

• aptitude for the management and resolution of conflicts;

• ability to analyse and resolve problems;

• adaptability and flexibility;

• ability to work also under pressure in a context that involves numerous challenges;

• ability to plan and organize the resources available;

• guidance on the continuous improvement of the quality of the services offered;

• reliability and personal responsibility;

• good psycho-physical ability and stress resistance;

• mastery in the use of different computer applications (RAISoft, computerized folders, etc.);

• unexceptionable and incensured conduct.

Conditions of recruitment

• Training, professional experience and attitudes, second

as provided by the collective agreement for the staff employed at the homes for the elderly and other institutions of the Canton Ticino (CCL ROCA).

• Class 30 CCL ROCA:

Minimum: CHF 87’315.-- yearly (to 100%) Maximum: CHF 114’872.-- yearly (to 100%) Including thirteenth monthly. In addition to the salary, family allowances according to LAFam are paid to the rightholders. Degree of employment 100% Flexible time and according to service requirements. From now on or from time to time. Documents to be produced 1. Letter of presentation and motivation; 2. curriculum vitae with photos; 3. diplomas, certificates of study and certificates of work; 4. references; 5. Judicial box extract*; 6. Excerpt from the Office for Executions and Failures*; 7. Medical certificate of suitability*** submitted through the form available on the website

* these documents may also be submitted at the time of the interview

** this document must be delivered in a closed envelope at the time of the interview. Any person who recognises himself in the profile and in the values sought, sends his application, accompanied by the documents requested, via online form accessible on the website www.ecam.swiss, by Tuesday 22 December 2026 at 4:00 pm. Applications supported by incomplete documentation will not be considered. There will be no valid offers and competition documents sent by ordinary mail or by e-mail. Applications reached by the end of 24.07.2026, date of the first notice of competition, shall not be submitted and shall be taken into account for the selection process. It is the faculty of the ECAM Governing Council to proceed to the pre-selection of the candidates through audits before the expiry of the competition. For further information, please contact the Vice-Director ECAM, Mrs Alessandra Pitozzi exclusively by sending notices to the address: resourceumane@ecam.swiss Mendrisio, 23 November 2026

